  "description": "Measures the cost of Gutch repository encryption. Both cases run the same Gutch release on the same runner with identical settings, a nominal 1 MiB FastCDC target, Zstd 3 and 8 MiB compressed bundles; only the second case encrypts its repository with AES-256-GCM, unlocked by a fixed local test password. Gutch relative compares unencrypted with encrypted Gutch. Fresh repositories and isolated caches. Four workers. One warm-up and 6 rotating measured repetitions; profiling off. Measurement contract 2 separates content repair, preserved-mtime damage, extra-file cleanup and full restoration. Strict source-derived SHA-256 validation follows every supported operation; both native and validation-inclusive durations are reported.",
